  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 579c9253f6a5be6499ca8a1851d07f90, type: 3}
  welcomeMessage: Welcome to Identifying the Alphabets Quiz.
  letsLearnMessage: In this quiz, you're going to type the Letters of the English
    Alphabets using Braille. Let's try typing them Alphabetically.
  completedMessage: Great Job! You finished Lesson 4 Identifying Alphabets.
  repeatQuestionMessage: Do you want to repeat again? Press repeat to repeat or next
    to finish.
  lessonCompleteMessage: You have finished learning the Alphabets. Do you want to
    repeat the lesson? Press repeat to repeat the lesson or press next to begin the
    quiz.
  lessonCompleteAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4b5843e386412ce4fae48c2af430b31a, type: 3}
  lessonPages:
  - title: Lesson 4
    lessonText: Welcome to Lesson 4, Identifying Alphabets.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b6ec0c3ba92714f4fb8eaaf8a20aa841, type: 3}
  - title: Identifying Alphabets
    lessonText: In this lesson, you will learn the letters of the alphabet, and how
      each letter is represented in Braille.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b7ec2ee1f635bdb459329deb81e08086, type: 3}
  - title: What is the Alphabet?
    lessonText: The English alphabet has 26 letters, from A to Z. We use these letters
      to form words, sentences, and stories. Learning the alphabet is the first step
      in reading and writing.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dfbce6171931db44882fe3b4ec853e18, type: 3}
  - title: How Braille Works
    lessonText: Every Braille letter is made using a pattern of six dots. Some dots
      are raised while others are not. Different combinations of raised dots create
      different letters.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 571b6cfb66ede7c47a95ca432cd023e1, type: 3}
  - title: Use of Controller
    lessonText: In your case we're going to press the dots in your controller to
      type a letter.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a19e4a020e2f7dc4683024ff4091e7ac, type: 3}
  - title: Braille Dots
    lessonText: The six Braille dots are numbered from 1 to 6. Learning these dot
      numbers helps you understand how each letter is formed.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a933a48796b7b8d4aa5a9acaedb5792c, type: 3}
  - title: Learning the Alphabet
    lessonText: Each letter of the alphabet has its own Braille pattern. During this
      lesson, you will learn which dots are used for every letter from A to Z.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7b94d760b7ea8f54db4ea511869fd88f, type: 3}
  - title: Let's Practice!
    lessonText: "Listen carefully to each instruction. You will learn one letter
      at a time, hear its sound, learn the Braille dots it uses, and then practice
      typing it yourself. Don't worry if you make a mistake\u2014you can always try
      again."
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 88a70e8689fbb3045843786f1b8d8437, type: 3}
  lessonLetters:
  - letter: 65
    categoryLabel: Letter
    displayImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b8df670c7e9957a45b35c5685879a322, type: 3}
    introductionMessage: The first letter in the english alphabet is Letter A.
    introAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 89fa9757d60c6d34aae8eb679cb6bc4c, type: 3}
    letterSoundMessage: Letter A sounds "Ahhhh".
    letterSoundAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7efb0b2b66bd6df47a13d723c25fd7a1, type: 3}
    brailleInstructionMessage: The letter A in Braille is typed using Dot 1.
    brailleInstructionAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cbfc3f166d63139409f64e5d9259f5f2, type: 3}
    promptMessage: Press dot 1 to type letter A.
    promptAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9b6554a67a0dcae41aab041357f98af7, type: 3}
    successMessage: That is Correct.
    successAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 806f9040f8926b94db47e2caef85d97b, type: 3}
    wrongMessage: That is wrong, Please Try Again.
    wrongAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dd615f4eef83e3b49b22a11445f9b6d6, type: 3}
    supportMessage: Remember Letter A uses Dot number 1. Press dot 1 to type Letter
      A.
    supportAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2be844648fc5ec04e905c429bfc32607, type: 3}
  - letter: 66
    categoryLabel: Letter
    displayImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cc6bae3515a12144da0cb8e13ecbcaad, type: 3}
    introductionMessage: The next letter is Letter B.
    introAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ba6f3ce4e21130343aad9123f4d5595b, type: 3}
    letterSoundMessage: Letter B sounds "b".
    letterSoundAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 00bfa39b482619544b06c984bb0cceaa, type: 3}
    brailleInstructionMessage: The letter B in Braille is typed using Dot 1, and
      2.
    brailleInstructionAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7c28cf0b730f6694391e7cef43dbef21, type: 3}
    promptMessage: Press dot 1 & 2 at the same time to type letter B.
    promptAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d8b5f609199140646ba7f4f58a34ebe2, type: 3}
    successMessage: That is Correct.
    successAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 806f9040f8926b94db47e2caef85d97b, type: 3}
    wrongMessage: That is wrong, Please Try Again.
    wrongAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dd615f4eef83e3b49b22a11445f9b6d6, type: 3}
    supportMessage: Remember Letter B uses Dot number 1&2. Press dot 1&2 at the same
      time to type Letter B.
    supportAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0d5a28974a840b841aa699ac53755af3, type: 3}
  - letter: 67
    categoryLabel: Letter
    displayImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f1f1d850f3dbd5e4387cef24e691c6dc, type: 3}
    introductionMessage: The next letter is Letter C.
    introAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fe0750ea528c7a9489532a90fcb9bc48, type: 3}
    letterSoundMessage: Letter C sounds "k" sometimes it sounds "s" depending on
      how it is used in a word.
    letterSoundAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bf01bcf0e88b3194e8cf9f8149c64591, type: 3}
    brailleInstructionMessage: The letter C in Braille is typed using Dot 1, and
      4.
    brailleInstructionAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6a50e5862bc22104b8715e367e75b242, type: 3}
    promptMessage: Press dot 1 & 4 at the same time to type letter C.
    promptAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8f3cf1c4b5628dc44859b730f020be38, type: 3}
    successMessage: That is Correct.
    successAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 806f9040f8926b94db47e2caef85d97b, type: 3}
    wrongMessage: That is wrong, Please Try Again.
    wrongAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dd615f4eef83e3b49b22a11445f9b6d6, type: 3}
    supportMessage: Remember Letter C uses Dot number 1&3. Press dot 1&3 at the same
      time to type Letter C.
    supportAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f8fa74582b7f9e5429db6e2ca0bff1f0, type: 3}
